questions.prompt:
A report exporter runs the method below. `ReportExportException` is a custom exception whose constructor stores its second argument as `InnerException`. During one call, `QueryRows` throws a `TimeoutException`. The `catch` block runs, and then `connection.Close()` in `finally` throws an `IOException`. No other code in the method catches exceptions.

```csharp
public void Export(DbConnection connection)
{
    try
    {
        QueryRows(connection);
    }
    catch (TimeoutException ex)
    {
        throw new ReportExportException("Export failed.", ex);
    }
    finally
    {
        connection.Close();
    }
}
```

Which exception reaches the caller of `Export`, and why does wrapping the timeout in the `catch` block not change that outcome?
